$DATUM Bromobenzene (53 μL, 0.5 mmol, 1 equiv) and 4-methoxyphenylmagnesium
bromide (1.25 mL, 0.63 mmol, 0.5 M in THF solution, 1.25 equiv). THF was
remove under vacuo until obtain approximately 0.6-0.7 mL of solvent. The
crude reaction mixture was purified TLC preparative hexane/EtOAct (98:2).
4-Methoxybiphenyl as white solid, yield 76 mg, 82%. 1H NMR (600 MHz,
CDCl3, 25°C): δ (ppm) 7.57-7.52 (m, 4H), 7.41 (t, J = 9 Hz, 2H), 7.30
(dt, J = 1.5 and 9 Hz, 1H), 6.97 (dt, J = 2 and 9 Hz, 2H), 3.84 (s, 3H);
13C NMR (150 MHz, CDCl3, 25°C): δ (ppm) 159.3, 141.0, 134.0, 128.9,
128.4, 126.9, 126.9, 114.4, 55.6.
