$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General procedure for compounds 6a-6i based on the Kumada cross coupling
reaction. The Grignard reagent 5 (6 mmol) was added drop wise at room
temperature to a suspension of 6-iodoquinazolinone 4 (2 mmol) and
NiCl2(dppe) (10 mol %) in THF (5 mL). The reaction mixture was stirred
for 3 h at room temperature. The process was monitored by TLC. Upon
completion of the reaction the mixture was quenched with water (5 mL) and
the salts were filtered off through Celite. The organic layer was dried
over anhydrous Na2SO4 and concentrated under reduced pressure to give the
crude products 6a-6i purified by silica gel column chromatography
(hexane-EtOAc, 9: 1). 3-Methyl-2,6-diphenylquinazolin-4(3H)-one (6a).
Yield 80%. mp 105-106°C. IR spectrum, ν, cm-1: 1680 (C=O). 1H NMR
spectrum, δ, ppm: 8.56 s (1H), 8.02 d (1H, J = 8.6 Hz), 7.82 d (1H, J =
8.6 Hz), 7.72 d (2H, J = 7.5 Hz), 7.47-7.60 m (7H), 7.38 m (1H), 3.53 s
(3H). 13C NMR spectrum, δC, ppm: 162.7, 155.9, 146.4, 139.8, 139.6,
135.3, 133.1, 130.0, 128.9, 128.8, 127.9, 127.8, 127.1, 124.5, 120.7,
34.1. ESI-HRMS [M + H]+ (m/z). Found 313.1343. C21H17N2O. Calculated
313.1263.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Kumada cross coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Kumada cross coupling reaction based synthesis, antimicrobial and
computational studies of 6-aryl-2-phenyl-3-methylquinazolin-4(3H)-ones
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Shankaraiah, P.; Veeresham, S.; Bhavani, A. K. D.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Russian Journal of General Chemistry (2016), 86(2), 368-375

