$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the KCT reaction A.
PICB-NHC-Ni catalyst 6b (14.5 mg to 19 mg, 0.00013 mmol, 0.25 mol% as Ni)
(loading of cat 6b is depending of the lot: 0.086 mmol/g to 0.066 mmol/g)
was placed in a Schlenk tube-type and heated with a hair dryer in vacuo
for 2 minutes. Aryl, Vinyl, or Alkyl halide (0.5 mmol, 1 equiv) and
Grignard reagents (0.63 mmol, 1.25 equiv) were introduced, and then the
solvent volume was adjusted with dried and degassed THF to a volume of
0.75 mL. The mixture was stirred for 12 h at room temperature. The
reaction was quenched by adding EtOH (0.5 mL). The catalyst was collected
by filtration using KIRIYAMAROHTO® funnel and washed with EtOAc. The
solution was hydrolyzed with saturated aqueous NH4Cl (10 mL) and the
aqueous phase was extracted with EtOAc (3 x 10 mL). The combined organic
phases were dried over MgSO4 and the solvent was removed in vacuo. The
residue was purified by TLC preparative. 3-bromo"tolyl (61 μL, 0.5 mmol,
1 equiv) and phenylmagnesium chloride (0.32 mL, 0.63 mmol, 2M in THF
solution, 1.25 equiv) in THF (0.35 mL). The crude reaction mixture was
purified TLC preparative hexane (100%). 3-Methylbiphenyl, yield 78%. GC
flow rate (157.4 kPa, He), Inject (100°C), Detect. (300°C), Int. T.
(100°C), Int. T. (0 min), Rate (10°C/min), Fin. T. (300°C), Fin. T. (10
min) : tR (min) 8.0 (3-bromo tolyl ), 10.0 (internal standart), 13.9
(product) ; 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3, 25°C): δ (ppm) 7.56 (q, J = 6 Hz,
2H), 7.45-7.35 (m, 4H), 7.33-7.28 (m, 2H), 7.23-7.21 (m, 1H), 7.14 (t, J
= 7 Hz, 1H), 2.40 (s,3H); 13C NMR (150 MHz, CDCl3, 25°C): δ (ppm) 141.9,
141.5, 138.4, 132.6, 129.0, 128.9, 128.9, 128.2, 128.1, 127.5, 127.4,
127.4, 124.5, 21.8.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM catalyst prepared and used, optimization study, catalyst is a reaction
product with a bromoalkyl polystyrene, nickel and DBU, optimized on
catalyst for yield
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Copolymer-Incarcerated Nickel Nanoparticles with N-Heterocyclic Carbene
Precursors as Active Cross-Linking Agents for Corriu-Kumada-Tamao
Reaction
