$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Kumada−Corriu
Reaction. Under argon, to the aryl halide (0.5 mmol) were added a
solution of 3 in dioxane (3 mg, 0.1 mL, 0.5 mol %) and
isopropenylmagnesium bromide (1.5 mL at 0.5 M in THF, 0.75 mmol). The
reaction mixture was stirred at room temperature for 12 h. Then the
solution was concentrated under reduced pressure and quenched with water
(2 mL), and the product was extracted with Et2O (3 x 2 mL). The combined
organic layers were dried over MgSO4, filtered, and concentrated under
reduced pressure. The crude product was finally purified by flash
chromatography on silica gel with ether/pentane as eluent (from 0.5/99.5
to 2/8). 1,3-Dimethoxy-2-(prop-1-en-2-yl)benzene (7c). Yield: 67 mg, 0.38
mmol, 75%. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 7.21 (t, J = 8.3 Hz, 1H), 6.60 (d,
J = 8.3 Hz, 2H), 5.36 (dd, J = 2.6, 1.0 Hz, 1H), 4.90 (dd, J = 2.1, 0.9
Hz, 1H), 3.83 (s, 6H), 2.05 (d, J = 1.0, 3H). 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3): δ
157.6, 139.7, 128.3, 121.8, 116.1, 104.4, 56.4, 23.8.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Kumada-Corriu reaction
