the Kumada cross coupling reaction. The Grignard reagent 5 (6 mmol) was
added drop wise at room temperature to a suspension of
6-iodoquinazolinone 4 (2 mmol) and NiCl2(dppe) (10 mol %) in THF (5 mL).
The reaction mixture was stirred for 3 h at room temperature. The process
was monitored by TLC. Upon completion of the reaction the mixture was
quenched with water (5 mL) and the salts were filtered off through
Celite. The organic layer was dried over anhydrous Na2SO4 and
concentrated under reduced pressure to give the crude products 6a-6i
purified by silica gel column chromatography (hexane-EtOAc, 9: 1).
6-(6-Methoxybenzo[b]thiophen-2-yl)-3-methyl-2-phenylquinazolin-4(3H)-one
(6i). Yield 75%. mp 205-206°C. IR spectrum, ν, cm-1: 1674 (C=O). 1H NMR
spectrum, δ, ppm: 8.59 d (1H, J = 2.0 Hz), 8.05 d (1H, J = 8.9 Hz), 7.76
d (1H, J = 7.9 Hz), 7.68 d (1H, J =7.9 Hz), 7.53-7.61 m (6H), 7.33 m
(1H), 7.03 d.d (1H, J = 8.9 Hz), 3.91 s (3H), 3.52 s (3H). 13C NMR
spectrum, δC, ppm: 162.5, 157.7, 156.0, 146.7, 141.2, 140.0, 135.2,
134.6, 133.3, 131.9, 130.1, 128.8, 128.1, 128.0, 124.4, 123.3, 120.8,
120.1, 114.8, 104.7, 55.6, 34.3. ESI-HRMS [M + H]+ (m/z). Found 399.1165.
C24H18N2O2S. Calculated 399.1089.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Kumada cross coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Kumada cross coupling reaction based synthesis, antimicrobial and
computational studies of 6-aryl-2-phenyl-3-methylquinazolin-4(3H)-ones
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Shankaraiah, P.; Veeresham, S.; Bhavani, A. K. D.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Russian Journal of General Chemistry (2016), 86(2), 368-375

