$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: (1). Representative Procedure for the Kumada
Coupling of Aryl Chlorides. A Schlenk tube was charged with nickel
complex 2 (0.05 mL, 0.05 M solution in THF, 0.0025 mmol), THF (1.5 mL),
and PhCl (0.056 g, 0.5 mmol). To the solution was added dropwise a
solution of p-MeC6H4MgBr (1.5 mL, 0.5 M in THF, 0.75 mmol) at 25 °C with
stirring. After stirring at this temperature for 24 h, the reaction
mixture was quenched with water and extracted with diethyl ether (3 × 10
mL). The combined organic phases were dried over Na2SO4, concentrated by
rotary evaporation, and purified by column chromatography (silica gel,
eluted using petroleum ether). p-MeC6H4Ph (0.084 g, 99%).
2-p-Tolylpyridine.36 1H NMR (CDCl3): δ 2.37 (s, 3H), 7.10-7.27 (m, 1H),
7.25 (d, J = 7.9 Hz, 2H), 7.65-7.67 (m, 2H), 7.88 (d, J = 8.1 Hz, 2H),
8.64-8.66 (m, 1H). 13C NMR (CDCl3): δ 21.38, 120.2, 121.8, 126.8, 129.5,
136.7, 139.0, 149.6, 157.5.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Kumada coupling, other catalyst gave higher yield
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Kumada Coupling of Aryl, Heteroaryl, and Vinyl Chlorides Catalyzed by
Amido Pincer Nickel Complexes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Liu, Ning; Wang, Zhong-Xia
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2011), 76(24), 10031-10038

